# 🐛 bug report

When using if-else cases to differentiate between e.g. browser and server but also for different build env, unused dependencies are not removed.

The code is not failing in any way, it is just bigger than it needs to be.

## 🎛 Configuration (.babelrc, package.json, cli command)

See https://github.com/garthenweb/parcel-bug-report-examples/tree/bug/dead-code-elemination-dependency-wrong-branch

## 🤔 Expected Behavior

Should remove all unused code.

## 😯 Current Behavior

Keeps the library code.

## 💁 Possible Solution

* insert Buffer library after dead code elimination?
* remove Buffer library after dead code elimination?
* find out that Buffer is not used and split it out?
* insert the Buffer library into the branch where it is used in?

## 💻 Code Sample

```javascript
const btoa = process.browser
  ? globalThis.btoa
  : (str) => Buffer.from(str.toString(), "binary").toString("base64");

console.log(btoa("test"));
```
https://github.com/garthenweb/parcel-bug-report-examples/blob/bug/dead-code-elemination-dependency-wrong-branch/src/index.js

The same happens for the following code

```javascript
import { act } from 'react-dom/test-utils'
const fireAsAct = (cb: () => void) => {
  if (process.env.NODE_ENV === "test") {
    act(() => cb());
  } else {
    cb();
  }
};

fireAsAct(() => console.log('test'));
```

For the latter example, I am actually not sure if it is a bug, as the `react-dom` does not have `sideeffects: false` set in package.json. But inserting the Buffer in the first example is unexpected.

Rewriting the `react-dom` example to the following works as expected
```javascript
const fireAsAct = (cb: () => void) => {
  if (process.env.NODE_ENV === "test") {
    const { act } = require("react-dom/test-utils");
    act(() => cb());
  } else {
    cb();
  }
};

fireAsAct(() => console.log('test'));
```

## 🌍 Your Environment

<!--- Include as many relevant details about the environment you experienced the bug in -->

| Software         | Version(s) |
| ---------------- | ---------- |
| Parcel           | 2.0.0-nightly.226
| Node             | v12.8.1
| npm         | v6.14.4
| Operating System | Windows (WSL v1/ Ubuntu Bash)

