I have the same issue, according to the docs **development-only features are supported** and [terser's `dead_code`](https://github.com/terser/terser#compress-options) facilitates them.

**But** this code has no removal effect:

```js
if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') { // Or, `process.env.NODE_ENV !== 'production'`
  // Only runs in development and should be stripped from production build.
  // But isn't stripped fromproductoin build...
}
```

> To take advantage of the same kind of development-only debugging features, ensure that [terser's `dead_code` option](https://github.com/terser/terser#compress-options) is on (it is by default) and wrap any development-only debugging in a conditional check like so:
https://parceljs.org/production.html#optimisations

Thanks @mischnic 

Yes, this is what I assumed too.

Here is how I got it working for my case (tree shaking/scope hoisting disabled):

`module-a.js` (did not work):
```js
import fatJson from './fat.json';

export function checkExistence(key) {
  if (process.env.NODE_ENV === "development") {
     // check stuff with fatJson ... 
  }

  return true;
}
```

`module-a.js` (works this way):
```js
export function checkExistence(key) {
  if (process.env.NODE_ENV === "development") {
    const fatJson = require('./fat.json');
     // check stuff with fatJson ... 
  }

  return true;
}
```

1. publish `module-a` on NPM
2. import in my app
3. build my app with parcel
4. production build now excludes the `fat.json`

> `module-a.js` (did not work):
> ```js
> import fatJson from './fat.json';
> 
> export function checkExistence(key) {
>   if (process.env.NODE_ENV === "development") {
>      // check stuff with fatJson ... 
>   }
> 
>   return true;
> }
> ```

This works in Parcel 2 if you add
```js
{
	"sideEffects": ["module-a.js"]
}
```
or (depending on the situation)
```js
{
	"sideEffects": false
}
```
so that the JSON file is marked as side-effect free.
